@startuml runtime_shell
title Operator Runtime Shell (ncr_runtime.exe)

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #2B4C7E
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EEF5FF

package "runtime_app (shell)" {
  class RuntimeShellWindow <<QMainWindow>> {
    ..pages..
    -buildProjectSelectPage()
    -buildRuntimePage()
    ..project lifecycle..
    -tryStartRememberedProject()
    -onBrowseForProject()
    -startProject(path) : bool
    -showProjectSelect(reason)
    ..runtime..
    -startTaskRuntimes()
    -stopTaskRuntimes()
    -applyCurrentLayout()
    {static} +kMaxTasks : int = 8
  }

  class RuntimeLayoutController {
    {static} +kMaxTiles : int = 8
    {static} +supportedTileCounts() : QList<int>
    {static} +smallestFittingTileCount(taskCount) : int
    {static} +gridFor(tileCount) : QSize
    {static} +applyLayout(manager, docks, tileCount)
  }
}

package "app (shell)" {
  class MainWindow <<QMainWindow>>
}

package "src (shared modules)" {
  class "vc::model::Project" as Project
  class "vc::model::ProjectRepository" as ProjectRepository
  class "vc::model::TaskLocalization" as TaskLocalization
  class LocalizationDashboardWidget <<ITaskWidget>>
  class "AppSettings" as AppSettings
  class "ThemeManager" as ThemeManager
}

package "3rdparty" {
  class "ads::CDockManager" as CDockManager
  class "ads::CDockWidget" as CDockWidget
}

RuntimeShellWindow --> RuntimeLayoutController : tile grid
RuntimeShellWindow --> Project : loads, never saves
RuntimeShellWindow ..> ProjectRepository : load() only
RuntimeShellWindow --> TaskLocalization : beginRuntime() / endRuntime()
RuntimeShellWindow *-- LocalizationDashboardWidget : one per task
RuntimeShellWindow --> AppSettings : lastRuntimeProjectPath
RuntimeShellWindow --> ThemeManager
RuntimeShellWindow *-- CDockManager
RuntimeLayoutController ..> CDockManager : addDockWidget placements
CDockManager *-- CDockWidget

MainWindow --> Project : loads AND saves

note bottom of RuntimeShellWindow
  Startup decision tree (three distinct messages,
  because they call for three different actions):
    remembered path empty  -> select page, "none run yet"
    file missing           -> select page, "moved/renamed/drive"
    load fails             -> select page, "could not be loaded: <reason>"
    load succeeds          -> runtime view, tasks already running

  The remembered path is written ONLY after a load
  succeeds, so a corrupt file never becomes the one
  the next launch tries first.

  Tasks enter runtime with no button press. A task that
  fails setup keeps its tile showing Faulted, and tasks
  past the 8 cap are named in the log and toolbar --
  a task nobody can see is a task nobody is watching.
end note

note right of RuntimeLayoutController
  ADS has docking and floating but no "tile into N"
  primitive, so the grid is an explicit sequence of
  addDockWidget() placements.
    1 -> 1x1   2 -> 1x2   4 -> 2x2
    6 -> 3x2   8 -> 4x2

  Floating is an operator decision and is never undone
  by a layout change: a floated dock is skipped and
  does not consume a tile. Floating is a VIEW
  operation -- a floated task keeps running.
end note

note bottom of MainWindow
  Phase 6 split the product into two shells by the
  project owner's decision, superseding the Phase 4
  "one executable" shape.

  They are PEERS over the same src/ modules, not a
  hierarchy: neither may include the other's headers.
  Shared qmake config lives in qmake/app_common.pri.

  Only this shell writes a project file. One writer,
  one reader -- which is why no project-file
  compatibility layer between them is needed.
end note

note bottom of LocalizationDashboardWidget
  Reused as-is by the runtime shell: read-only, driven
  purely by task signals.

  LocalizationTaskWidget is deliberately NOT reused --
  it starts Commission on the task in its constructor,
  which would put the operator executable into
  commissioning on launch.
end note

@enduml
